The mean-zero triangular Green function has the expansion $$\label{cal:green-series}
 h_\triangle(z)=-\log|z|+C_\triangle+\frac{\pi|z|^2}{2}
                 +\sum_{m\ge1}c_m\operatorname{Re}(z^{6m}),
 \qquad 0<|z|<a,$$ where $C_\triangle$ is its regular part at the origin. The series and all of its derivatives converge locally away from $|z|=a$.

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $S^2=\{y\in\mathbb R^3:\|y\|=1\}$ be the unit sphere. For each integer $n\ge2$, define $$E_{\log}(n)=\min_{(y_1,\ldots,y_n)\in(S^2)^n}
 \left(-\sum_{\substack{1\le i,j\le n\\i\ne j}}
              \log\|y_i-y_j\|\right),$$ where the sum is over ordered pairs, $\|\cdot\|$ is the Euclidean norm in $\mathbb R^3$, $\log$ is the natural logarithm, and a collision has energy $+\infty$. Then, as $n\to\infty$ through the integers, $$\label{eq:bhs-asymptotic}
E_{\log}(n)=\left(\frac12-\log2\right)n^2
             -\frac n2\log n+C_{\mathrm{BHS}}n+o(n),$$ where $$\label{eq:bhs-constant}
C_{\mathrm{BHS}}
=2\log2+\frac12\log\!\left(\frac23\right)
       +3\log\!\left(\frac{\sqrt\pi}{\Gamma(1/3)}\right),$$ and $\Gamma$ is Euler’s gamma function.

Let $\Lambda\subset\mathbb R^2$ be simple and locally finite, and let $E\in\mathcal D'(\mathbb R^2;\mathbb R^2)$ be a distributional vector field satisfying $$\operatorname{div}E=2\pi\Bigl(\sum_{p\in\Lambda}\delta_p-1\Bigr),
 \qquad \operatorname{curl}E=0.$$ The field is smooth off $\Lambda$. Near each $p\in\Lambda$ it has the form $$\label{red:local-expansion}
 E(x)=\frac{x-p}{|x-p|^2}+F_p(x),\qquad F_p\text{ smooth}.$$ Consequently $E$ has a representative in $L^q_{\mathrm{loc}}$ for every $1\le q<2$, and $W(E,\xi)$ exists as a finite real number for every smooth compactly supported $\xi$.

The mean-zero triangular Green function has the expansion $$\label{cal:green-series}
 h_\triangle(z)=-\log|z|+C_\triangle+\frac{\pi|z|^2}{2}
                 +\sum_{m\ge1}c_m\operatorname{Re}(z^{6m}),
 \qquad 0<|z|<a,$$ where $C_\triangle$ is its regular part at the origin. The series and all of its derivatives converge locally away from $|z|=a$.
